`get`: look the key up in `index_`, splice that node to the front of `order_` (list iterators survive `splice`), then return the value through the same iterator.
```cpp
auto it = index_.find(key);
if (it == index_.end()) return std::nullopt;
order_.splice(order_.begin(), order_, it->second);
return it->second->second;
```

Evict at the end of the new-key path, map entry first because `pop_back` destroys the key you need:
```cpp
if (order_.size() > cap_) {
    index_.erase(order_.back().first);
    order_.pop_back();
}
```
`contains` is `index_.count(key) > 0`, `size` is `order_.size()`, and `keys_mru_first` walks `order_` front to back pushing each `.first`.
